Rule 1 (parameters a and b must be strictly positive for the log-beta function to be defined)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= min(v_1) > 0 ∧ min(v_2) > 0
>>
Rule 2 (scalar parameters a and b must be strictly positive)
{v_1 : int ⊎ float, v_2 : int ⊎ float} |= v_1 > 0 ∧ v_2 > 0
>>
Rule 3 (tensors a and b must have matching data types)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)
>>
Rule 4 (tensors a and b must be real-valued)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≥ 1 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 8
